  (history ("claude" "2026-09-28" "Glasswood SOUND: the fixed moment in Blue Hall (first visit), the first cave the moths light. A low D alone in the dark and a glint in the ice; the moths gather, chiming in H3's own partials (A5 C#6 E6 A6 C#7 E7), sparse and then close; a pad swells like light spreading on the walls (D, E/D, D, in D Lydian); an ice bell climbs H3's chord, A C# E, leans on G# and B, and settles on A. It thins as the moths settle; a silent 6 s pattern lets it ring out.")))
